{"type":"standard","title":"Roy Cooper","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Roy Cooper</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7372694","titles":{"canonical":"Roy_Cooper","normalized":"Roy Cooper","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Roy Cooper</span></span>"},"pageid":576683,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":439},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Roy_Cooper_at_Roy_Cooper_Rally_April_2026-2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2177,"height":2899},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377298352","tid":"e4894d86-bb74-11f1-ab33-9a443f48fc90","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:43:35Z","description":"Governor of North Carolina from 2017 to 2025","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Roy_Cooper"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Roy_Cooper","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy_Cooper?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Roy_Cooper"}},"extract":"Roy Asberry Cooper III is an American politician and lawyer who was the 75th governor of North Carolina from 2017 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the 50th attorney general of North Carolina from 2001 to 2017 and served in the North Carolina General Assembly from 1987 to 2001.","extract_html":"<p><b>Roy Asberry Cooper III</b> is an American politician and lawyer who was the 75th governor of North Carolina from 2017 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the 50th attorney general of North Carolina from 2001 to 2017 and served in the North Carolina General Assembly from 1987 to 2001.</p>"}